<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n2806" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἰχμ-ητής</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οῦ</span>, 
			Dor.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἰχμ-ᾱτάς</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾶ</span>, ὁ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἰχμή</span>) poet., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>spearman, warrior</i>, esp. opp. to archers, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				2.543
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				2.19
			</span></i>, al., <i><span class="en">
				Archil.
				119
			</span></i>, cj.in <i><span class="en">
				Alcm.
				68
			</span></i>,etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> In Pi.as
				Adj., </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b>
			<i>pointed</i> (or <i>spear-wielding</i>), 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἰ. κεραυνός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>P.</u>
					1.5
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>warlike</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἰ. θυμός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>N.</u>
					9.37
				</span></i>
			:—fem. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἴχμητις</span></b>  (sic), <i><span class="en">
				<u>EM</u>
				595.39
			</span></i>.</div>
